# Checkout with LF line endings on every platform. Windows git defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would write CRLF: the skill's YAML frontmatter and the
# validator's anchored matches both break on CRLF, so the repository pins the
# line ending instead of trusting each machine's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
